  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "22c739ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "By default, pandas hides columns if your table is too wide to fit on screen. This tells it: show all columns, don't truncate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "f10ea0d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pd.set_option('display.max_columns',None)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "118d271e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Sets a default chart size (10 inches wide, 6 tall) so you don't have to specify it every time you plot something."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 27,
   "id": "0a0c4e40",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize']= (10, 6)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "41f4845b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Sets a visual style for charts \u2014 white background with light gridlines, easier to read than the plain default."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "613dfaf3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sns.set_style('whitegrid')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "id": "fa0f7902",
