      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "Empty DataFrame\n",
       "Columns: [DATE, STORE_NBR, LYLTY_CARD_NBR, TXN_ID, PROD_NBR, PROD_NAME, PROD_QTY, TOT_SALES, PACK_SIZE, BRAND]\n",
       "Index: []"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 53,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "outlier_customer = transactions.loc[transactions['PROD_QTY'] > 100, 'LYLTY_CARD_NBR']\n",
    "transactions[transactions['LYLTY_CARD_NBR'].isin(outlier_customer)]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b36dab9a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Remove the outlier customer's transactions if they look like a commercial buyer, not a regular shopper"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "id": "8e33d4ea",
   "source": [
    "Remove all of that customer's transactions from the dataset, since their buying pattern looks like a business/bulk buyer rather than a typical household \u2014 including them would distort the analysis."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 54,
   "id": "78a323d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "(255510, 10)"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 54,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "transactions = transactions[~transactions['LYLTY_CARD_NBR'].isin(outlier_customer)].copy()\n",
    "transactions.shape"
   ]
  },
